BigIris built with the `ai` feature includes image-engine-native
(https://github.com/biglinux/image-engine-native, revision
adbe1784bafd9329c8d667f28759aedfbf841d29): the native-engine,
native-vulkan, birefnet-native, realesrgan-native, scunet-native and
lama-native crates, MIT-licensed, with parts under BSD-3-Clause. Their
license and notices follow.

The model weights are not part of BigIris. They are installed by the
BigLinux packages birefnet-native (BiRefNet-lite, MIT), realesrgan-native
(Real-ESRGAN, BSD-3-Clause), scunet-native (SCUNet, Apache-2.0) and
lama-native (Big LaMa, Apache-2.0), each with its license under
/usr/share/licenses/<package>.

